description: "\"guarantees[5]: Explicit Engineering Tradeoffs,Explainable Decisions,Context-Aware Optimization,Reusable Engineering Wisdom,Production-Oriented Reasoning\""
spec:
  id: tradeoff_types
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: Defines the complete ontology of engineering tradeoffs. A tradeoff represents the balancing of competing engineering objectives under a specific set of constraints. Every significant engineering decision should identify the tradeoffs that influenced the chosen solution.
purpose: Represent tradeoffs as first-class engineering knowledge objects that explain why one solution was selected over another.
ekr: "\"\\\"Every Engineering Knowledge Record contains\\\"[5]: Competing Objectives,Tradeoff Analysis,Chosen Balance,Rejected Alternatives,Expected Consequences\""
examples:
  Example_01:
    Decision: Use Redis Cache
    Gains: Lower Latency
    Sacrifice: Eventual Consistency
  Example_02:
    Decision: Microservices
    Gains: Independent Deployment
    Sacrifice: Operational Complexity
  Example_03:
    Decision: Rust
    Gains: Memory Safety
    Sacrifice: Learning Curve
  Example_04:
    Decision: Large Context Window
    Gains: Better Reasoning
    Sacrifice: Higher Inference Cost
success: Every engineering decision explains why competing alternatives were rejected.
future:
  multi_objective_optimization: true
  tradeoff_graphs: true
  adaptive_reasoning: true
  probabilistic_tradeoffs: true
  automated_decision_support: true
